the council agreed on a general approach  on updated rules for the training and  qualifications of professional Orion bus  drivers  this update puts greater emphasis on  safety in the training and will improve  recognition of qualifications across the  European Union the maritime conclusions  identify competitiveness the  carbonization and the digitalization as  guiding principles for a policy in this  area the rule saves the conclusion set a  target of having the number of serious  injuries on roads in the European Union  by 2030 from the 2020 baseline ministers  discussed work on enabling the  International Maritime Organization to  adopt an ambitious and ambitious initial  strategy in 2018 to reduce greenhouse  gas emissions from ships ministers also  expressed their initial views on the  mobility package a generally welcome the  Commission's efforts to clarify the  existing rules and step up enforcement  our very some key parts of the package  will need detailed assessment in respect  of their social economic and also in  some cases the environmental impact let  me be very clear social conditions of  road drivers are at the heart of our  concerns and our proposals aim at  improving the enforcement of EU social  rules and workers rights and road safety  cannot and will not be compromised in  any way the Commission has set out an  agenda to make clean competitive and  connected mobility a reality for all
 

